# IntraCore: параметры HAL блока из базы STM32CubeMX (db/mcu/IP/*_Modes.xml).
# Порождено tools/hal_import — руками не править. Формат: src/Docs/Description/HalCatalogFormat.md
[Ip]
Name=MDF
Version=v1_0_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
MDF_Instance0|MDF_Instance0|MDFgroup||||
MDF_Handle0|MDF_Handle0|MDFgroup||||
MDF_SITF0_ActivationSerialInterface|SITF0 Activation|||||
MDF_SITF0_Mode_Display|Serial interface mode|||||<b>Normal SPI </b>Mode <b>LF Master SPI </b>Mode : Dedicated to low-power use-cases, using low-speed sensors. To guarantee optimal timing performances, the application must select the same clock than the one provided to the external sensor for each SITFx <b>Manchester </b>Mode : Decoded data and clock signals are recovered from serial stream after Manchester decoding.
MDF_SITF0_Mode|MDF_SITF_Mode|||||
MDF_SITF0_Manchester_Front|Means of edge|||||Means of edge for Manchester Mode
MDF_SITF0_Threshold|Manchester symbol threshold|||4|31|Manchester symbol threshold.
MDF_SITF0_ClockSource|Serial interface clock source|||||Select which common clock source is used for the Serial Interface SITF
MDF_DFLT0_SITF_Choice|bitstream matrix Serial-ITF selection|||||Selection of the serial interface (SITF) to use for the current Filter configuration (DFLT) as well as the related Short Circuit Detector (SCD)
MDF_DFLT0_FilterBistreamFront|bitstream matrix Front selection|||||Select the bitstream to use. Indeed for each SITF the both streams are available (one defined on the rising edge, one defined on the falling edge).
MDF_DFLT0_FilterBistream|Filter Bitstream Selection|||||
MDF_DFLT0_StructureName|Structure|||||
MDF_DFLT0_Data_Source|Data Source|||||The source of the digital filter (DFLT) can be selected between the two following: • data coming from the Bitstream matrix (then select which SITF and the front used in the additionnal parameters) • data coming from the ADC interface 1 or 2 To use the data source coming from ADC interface 1 or 2, these 3 conditions have to be checked : - 1 : ADC1 (or ADC2) has to be activated with the Conversion Data Management Parameter set to "MDF mode" value - 2 : the SCD (Short Circuit Detector) mode has to be desactivated
MDF_DFLT0_CIC_Mode|CIC Mode|||||The Cascaded-Integrator-Comb (CIC) filter is a high-resolution low-pass decimation filter CIC filter can be configured with Sinc4 or Sinc5 order
MDF_DFLT0_ReshapeFilterActivation|Reshape Filter|||||Activation of reshaping filter mainly dedicated to the audio application but also usable in other applications.
MDF_DFLT0_ReshapeFilterDecimationRatio|Decimation ratio|||||The samples at the reshape filter output can be decimated by four (4) or not (1)
MDF_DFLT0_HighPassFilterActivation|High pass filter|||||"The high-pass filter suppresses the low-frequency content from the final output data stream in case of continuous conversion mode. This filter is useful when there is parasitic low-frequency noise (or DC signal) in the input data source and it must be removed from the final data."
MDF_DFLT0_HighPassCutOffFrequency|Cut off frequency|||||Cut-off freqency of the high-pass filter : FPCM represents the sampling frequency at HPF input
MDF_DFLT0_IntegratorActivation|Offset|||||The Integrator performs additional decimation and a resolution increase of data coming from the digital filter.
MDF_DFLT0_IntegratorValue|Integrator Value|||2|128|Value is the amount of integrated values.
MDF_DFLT0_IntegratorOutputDivision|Integrator Output division|||||In order to control the data width at the integrator output, the resulting data can be divided by 1, 4, 32 or 128.
MDF_DFLT0_SADActivation|Sound Activity|||||
MDF_DFLT0_SADDetector|Detector Mode|||||Sound activity detector mode.
MDF_DFLT0_SADFrameSize|Frame size|||||Size of one frame to compute short-term signal level.
MDF_DFLT0_SADHysteresis|Hysteresis|||||
MDF_DFLT0_SADTriggerEvent|Sound trigger event configuration|||||Sound trigger event configuration : An event indicates when the Sound Activity Detector (SAD) enters and/or exits the DETECT state. This event is used to generate an interrupt when a sound is detected or when a sound is no longer detected. Either the application receives an event only when the SAD enters the DETECT state (or MONITOR state). Or the application receives an event when the SAD enters or exits the DETECT state.
MDF_DFLT0_SADDataMemoryTransfer|Data Memory Transfer|||||
MDF_DFLT0_SADMinNoiseLevel|Minimum noise level|||0|8191|
MDF_DFLT0_SADHangoverWindow|hangover time window|||||Hangover time window in frames
MDF_DFLT0_SADLearningFrames|Learning frames|||||Number of learning frames for the first estimation of noise level.
MDF_DFLT0_SADAmbientNoiseSlope|Ambient Noise Slope|||0|7|Ambient noise slope control.
MDF_DFLT0_SADSignalNoiseThreshold|Signal Noise Threshold|||||Signal to noise threshold.
MDF_DFLT0_SADSoundLevelInterrupt|Sound level interrupt|||||This interrupt is mainly used for debug purpose.
MDF_DFLT0_AcquisitionMode|Acquisition mode|||||<b>Asynchronous, continuous</b> mode allows the application to start a continuous acquisition <b>Asynchronous, single-shot</b> mode allows the application to start the acquisition of one sample <b>Synchronous, continuous</b> mode allows the application to start a continuous acquisition by using trigger source <b>Synchronous, single-shot</b> mode allows the application to start a single acquisition by using trigger source <b>Window, continuous</b> mode allows the application to start or stop a continuous acquisition by consecutive edges of using trigger source <b>Window, snapshot (for MDF)</b> mode allows the application to store when a trigger occurs, the last valid sample, the current decimation value of CIC and the sample counter of the integrator are stored whereas the DFLT is continuously acquiring the samples
MDF_DFLT0_TriggerSource|Trigger Source|||||Digital filter trigger signal selection, select which external signals trigger for the corresponding filter When the trigger source is TRGO, the sensitivity is forced to falling edge.
MDF_DFLT0_TriggerEdge|Trigger edge|||||Edge to use on the trigger source. When the trigger source is TRGO, the sensitivity is forced to falling edge.
MDF_DFLT0_SnapShotFormat|Snapshot data resolution|||||
MDF_DFLT0_SCDActivation|Short Circuit Detector Activation|||||The SCD detects, with a very fast response time, if an analog signal reached saturated values (out-of-full scale ranges) and remained on this value for a given time.
MDF_DFLT0_SCDThreshold|Threshold|||2|256|Threshold defines the max consecutive 1's or 0's which will generate an event.
MDF_DFLT0_SCDBreakSignal|Break Signal|||||Break signal defines the signal to use when the threshold is reached.
MDF_DFLT0_OLDActivation|Out-Off Limit Detector Activation|||||"The OLD triggers an event when a signal reaches or crosses given maximum and minimum threshold values. The generated event drives a break signals when conditions are met. <b>Warning :</b> The OLD can be used only if the CIC filter is configured in motor and sensing mode (not vailable for CIC Mode = Sinc4 or Sinc5)"
MDF_DFLT0_OLDCicMode|OutOff Limit CIC Mode|||||CIC filter can be configured with Sinc1, Sinc2, Sinc3 or FastSinc order.
MDF_DFLT0_OLDDecimationRatio|Decimantion Ratio|||1|32|Decimation ration of the OLD CIC filter.
MDF_DFLT0_OLDEventConfig|OutOff Limit Event Config|||||Define when the OLD generates an event.
MDF_DFLT0_OLDBreakSignal|Break Signal|||||Break signal defines the signal to use when the threshold is reached.
MDF_DFLT0_OLDHighThreshold|High Threshold|||=MDF_DFLT0_OLDLowThreshold + 1|33554431|High Threshold for out-of-limit detector. Has to be strictly greater than Low Threshold Min = Low Threshold + 1 Max = 33554431
MDF_DFLT0_OLDLowThreshold|Low Threshold|||-33554432|=MDF_DFLT0_OLDHighThreshold - 1|Low Threshold for out-of-limit detector. Has to be strictly lower than High Threshold Min = -33554432 Max = High Threshold - 1
MDF_Handle1|MDF_Handle1|MDFgroup||||
MDF_Instance1|MDF_Instance1|MDFgroup||||
MDF_SITF1_ActivationSerialInterface|SITF1 Activation|||||
MDF_SITF1_Mode_Display|Serial interface mode|||||<b>Normal SPI </b>Mode <b>LF Master SPI </b>Mode : Dedicated to low-power use-cases, using low-speed sensors. To guarantee optimal timing performances, the application must select the same clock than the one provided to the external sensor for each SITFx <b>Manchester </b>Mode : Decoded data and clock signals are recovered from serial stream after Manchester decoding.
MDF_SITF1_Mode|MDF_SITF_Mode|||||
MDF_SITF1_Manchester_Front|Means of edge|||||Means of edge for Manchester Mode
MDF_SITF1_Threshold|Manchester symbol threshold|||4|31|Manchester symbol threshold.
MDF_SITF1_ClockSource|Serial interface clock source|||||Warning : The clock source used by the SITF is defined only in the Mode window. Here is just for information.
MDF_DFLT1_SITF_Choice|bitstream matrix Serial-ITF selection|||||Selection of the serial interface (SITF) to use for the current Filter configuration (DFLT) as well as the related Short Circuit Detector (SCD)
MDF_DFLT1_FilterBistreamFront|bitstream matrix Front selection|||||Select the bitstream to use. Indeed for each SITF the both streams are available (one defined on the rising edge, one defined on the falling edge).
MDF_DFLT1_FilterBistream|Filter Bitstream Selection|||||
MDF_DFLT1_Data_Source|Data Source|||||The source of the digital filter (DFLT) can be selected between the two following: • data coming from the Bitstream matrix (then select which SITF and the front used in the additionnal parameters) • data coming from the ADC interface 1 To use the data source coming from ADC interface 1, these 3 conditions have to be checked : - 1 : ADC1 has to be activated with the Conversion Data Management Parameter set to "MDF mode" value - 2 : the SCD (Short Circuit Detector) mode has to be desactivated
MDF_DFLT1_CIC_Mode|CIC Mode|||||The Cascaded-Integrator-Comb (CIC) filters are an efficient implementation of low-pass filters, often used for decimation and interpolation. CIC filter can be configured: – in single CIC filter with Sinc4 or Sinc5 order (for high-resolution low-pass decimation filter usually selected for audio applications, such as speech capture from digital microphones) – in two CIC filters with Sinc1, Sinc2, Sinc3 or FastSinc order (to offer a main filter path for acquisition and an auxiliary filter for fast-event generation (for the out-off-limit detector - OLD))
MDF_DFLT1_ReshapeFilterActivation|Reshape Filter|||||Activation of reshaping filter mainly dedicated to the audio application but also usable in other applications.
MDF_DFLT1_ReshapeFilterDecimationRatio|Decimation ratio|||||The samples at the reshape filter output can be decimated by four (4) or not (1)
MDF_DFLT1_HighPassFilterActivation|High pass filter|||||"The high-pass filter suppresses the low-frequency content from the final output data stream in case of continuous conversion mode. This filter is useful when there is parasitic low-frequency noise (or DC signal) in the input data source and it must be removed from the final data."
MDF_DFLT1_HighPassCutOffFrequency|Cut off frequency|||||Cut-off freqency of the high-pass filter : FPCM represents the sampling frequency at HPF input
MDF_DFLT1_IntegratorActivation|Integrator|||||The Integrator performs additional decimation and a resolution increase of data coming from the digital filter.
MDF_DFLT1_IntegratorValue|Integrator Value|||2|128|Value is the amount of integrated values.
MDF_DFLT1_IntegratorOutputDivision|Integrator Output division|||||In order to control the data width at the integrator output, the resulting data can be divided by 1, 4, 32 or 128.
MDF_DFLT1_SADActivation|Sound Activity|||||
MDF_DFLT1_SADDetector|Detector|||||Sound activity detector mode.
MDF_DFLT1_SADFrameSize|Frame size|||||Size of one frame to compute short-term signal level.
MDF_DFLT1_SADHysteresis|Hysteresis|||||
MDF_DFLT1_SADTriggerEvent|Sound trigger event configuration|||||Sound trigger event configuration : An event indicates when the Sound Activity Detector (SAD) enters and/or exits the DETECT state. This event is used to generate an interrupt when a sound is detected or when a sound is no longer detected. Either the application receives an event only when the SAD enters the DETECT state (or MONITOR state). Or the application receives an event when the SAD enters or exits the DETECT state.
MDF_DFLT1_SADDataMemoryTransfer|Data Memory Transfer|||||
MDF_DFLT1_SADMinNoiseLevel|Minimum noise level|||0|8191|
MDF_DFLT1_SADHangoverWindow|hangover time window|||||Hangover time window in frames
MDF_DFLT1_SADLearningFrames|Learning frames|||||Number of learning frames for the first estimation of noise level.
MDF_DFLT1_SADAmbientNoiseSlope|Ambient Noise Slope|||0|7|Ambient noise slope control.
MDF_DFLT1_SADSignalNoiseThreshold|Signal Noise Threshold|||||Signal to noise threshold.
MDF_DFLT1_SADSoundLevelInterrupt|Sound level interrupt|||||This interrupt is mainly used for debug purpose.
MDF_DFLT1_AcquisitionMode|Acquisition mode|||||<b>Asynchronous, continuous</b> mode allows the application to start a continuous acquisition <b>Asynchronous, single-shot</b> mode allows the application to start the acquisition of one sample <b>Synchronous, continuous</b> mode allows the application to start a continuous acquisition by using trigger source <b>Synchronous, single-shot</b> mode allows the application to start a single acquisition by using trigger source <b>Window, continuous</b> mode allows the application to start or stop a continuous acquisition by consecutive edges of using trigger source <b>Window, snapshot</b> mode allows the application to store when a trigger occurs, the last valid sample, the current decimation value of CIC and the sample counter of the integrator are stored whereas the DFLT is continuously acquiring the samples
