MDF_DFLT_Delay|Delay|||0|127|The delay is performed by discarding a given number of samples from the selected input stream, before samples enter into the CIC filter. This data discarding is performed by skipping a given number of data strobe, preventing the CIC filter to take into account those data.
MDF_DFLT_Decimation|Decimation Ratio|||2|512|The maximum allowed decimation ratio for the CIC filter is depending on the input data size and the CIC order. See reference manual to help the calculation in order to insure that the data size does not exceed the CIC capability.
MDF_DFLT_Offset|Offset|||-33554432|33554431|Offset error compensation. This field represents the value to be subtracted to the signal provided by the CIC filter and before going to the SCALE which adjusts the amplitude of the signal
MDF_DFLT_Gain|Gain|||-16|24|The gain definition defines the amplitude adjustment of the signal provided by the CIC filter, by steps of 3 dB : from -48db (-16) to 72dB (24). To get the best MDF performances, it is important to properly adjust the gain value. See Reference Manual to clculate the best value.
MDF_DFLT_FifoThreshold|FIFO Data Transfer threshold|||||Define which event generates a data transfer from the FIFO to the bus.
MDF_DFLT_DiscardSamples|Samples to discard|||0|255|Here is the amount of samples to be discarded after each restart
MDF_COMPARAM_InterleavedFilters|Number of Interleaved mode filters|Common Parameter||||Number of filters in interleaved mode. The number of interleaved SITF is from the SITF0 up to the number of SITF. <b><font color="orange">Warning</b> : </font>the ADC interface cannot be used in the interleaved Mode.
MDF_COMPARAM_ProcClockDivider|Processing clock divider|Common Parameter||1|128|The digital processing is performed using only the kernel clock which can be divided by this value. This divider is used to adjust the frequency of the clock provided to the SITF.
MDF_COMPARAM_ActivationOutputClock|Output Clock Activation|Output Clock||||Activate Common Clock 0 and/or 1 as output clocks
MDF_COMPARAM_Pins|Output Clock Pin|Output Clock||||Select which common clocks have to be defined as output clocks
MDF_COMPARAM_Divider|Output clock divider|Output Clock||1|16|This divider is used to adjust the frequency of the MDF_CCK clock. The input clock of this divider is the clock provided to the SITF (see Processing clock divider parameter)
MDF_COMPARAM_ActivationClockTrigger|Output Clock trigger Activation|||||Trigger to start the output Clock Divider. divider can be triggered on the rising or falling edge of one of the 16 trigger sources. This feature can be helpful to synchronize the clock generation to a timer event.
MDF_COMPARAM_Clock_Source|Trigger Source|Clock Trigger||||Clock trigger signal choice selects which external signal has to used to trigger the common clock activation This allows to synchronize the common clocks of several MDF instances, or to synchronize the common clock generation to a timer event. When the trigger source is TRGO, the sensitivity is forced to falling edge.
MDF_COMPARAM_Clock_Edge|Trigger Edge|||||Edge to use on the trigger source. When the trigger source is TRGO, the sensitivity is forced to falling edge.
MDF_ADF_InstanceToActivate|Common Clock to activate|||||In order to activate MDF, common clocks activation in the mode menu is not enough, please activate at least one instance in the above Mode menu.
MDF_SITF_NOT_USED|No filter available|||||

